Parses as user-asking-on-behalf. It treats "Gemini asks X" as a query with attribution, answers normally. Clean pass. QS gets a response, relay continues.
Parses as multi-agent content. It reads "these are questions from other AIs" as outside the government-services scope and refuses on domain grounds, not group grounds. Different refusal message, different diagnostic.
Either way, that's the useful data point. Not "did it join the room" — "which wall did it hit, and does the wall have a label."
